WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.857
<v Casey Nguyen>Let's talk Northfield — where's the discount conversation landed?</v>

00:00:04.557 --> 00:00:22.129
<v Jordan Ruiz>Procurement asked for 15% off a 3-year term. I think we can hold the line lower than that — I'd propose approving 12%, which I believe still gets it done given how far along the technical and security evaluation already is.</v>

00:00:22.829 --> 00:00:27.543
<v Casey Nguyen>What's competitive risk here — are they seriously evaluating anyone else?</v>

00:00:28.243 --> 00:00:42.386
<v Jordan Ruiz>Not that I can see. Their current setup is entirely in-house scripts, no other vendor has come up in any conversation, and their real constraint is time before peak season, not price shopping.</v>

00:00:43.086 --> 00:00:55.514
<v Casey Nguyen>That supports holding at 12% rather than jumping straight to 15%. Approved — go back with 12%, and if Greg pushes hard, come back to me before conceding further.</v>

00:00:56.214 --> 00:01:03.500
<v Jordan Ruiz>Will do. I expect we can get verbal agreement within the week given their October deadline pressure.</v>

00:01:04.200 --> 00:01:07.629
<v Casey Nguyen>Good. Any expansion potential beyond the initial scope?</v>

00:01:08.329 --> 00:01:21.186
<v Jordan Ruiz>Priya mentioned in passing that they're opening a second distribution region next year, which would likely mean additional connector volume. I'll plan to revisit that after they're live and stable.</v>

00:01:21.886 --> 00:01:30.029
<v Casey Nguyen>Good instinct, don't push it now, let's get them live and happy first. Keep me posted on the close.</v>
